(a) Prohibition. It shall be unlawful and shall be held a violation of this article for any person, group of persons, regardless of number, to willfully make, continue, or cause to be made or continued any loud, raucous and disturbing noise, which shall mean any sound which, because of its volume level, duration and character, annoys, disturbs, injures or endangers the comfort, health, peace or safety of reasonable persons of ordinary reason sensibilities within the county. The term "loud, raucous and disturbing noise" is limited to loud, raucous and disturbing noises heard on the public streets, on any public property, school or other public building or grounds thereof when in use, in any church, hospital or grounds thereof when occupied, or in or upon any residential property which is not the source of such noise.
(b) Evaluation. In determining whether a noise is unreasonably loud, raucous and disturbing, the following factors incident to such noise shall be considered:
(1) Time of day;
(2) Proximity to residences;
(3) Whether the noise is recurrent, intermittent, or constant;
(4) The volume and intensity;
(5) Whether the noise has been enhanced in volume or range by any electronic or mechanical means;
(6) The character and population density of the area; and
(7) Whether the noise is subject to being controlled without unreasonable effort or expense to the creator thereof.
(c) Declared nuisances. The following acts are declared to be nuisances in violation of this article, but this enumeration shall not be deemed to be exclusive:
(1) Prohibited hours for noises. Making loud, raucous and disturbing noise or sound between the hours of 9:00 p.m. and 7:00 a.m., if such noise is plainly audible across any residential property line shall be held to be prima facie evidence of a violation of this article; and
(2) Continuation of noise after notice. Continuing to make, create or knowingly assist in creating a loud, raucous and disturbing noise or sound after receiving actual notice that such noises or sounds are disturbing residents or other persons in the vicinity shall be held to be prima facie evidence of a violation of this article.
(d) Exemption. The following shall be exempt from the application of this article:
(1) Agricultural and horticultural. Noise resulting from agricultural and horticultural operations conducted in a reasonable manner and during reasonable hours;
(2) Authorized emergency vehicles. Noise resulting from any authorized emergency or public safety vehicle when responding to an emergency call or acting in the time of an emergency;
(3) Safety, warning signals. Noise of safety signals, warning devices and emergency pressure valves;
(4) Emergency repair. Noise resulting from emergency work needed to restore property to a safe condition after a fire, accident or natural disaster, or to restore public utilities;
(5) Motor vehicles. Noise from motor vehicles in proper operating condition and properly equipped with the manufacturers' standard mufflers and noise reducing equipment;
(6) Military or law enforcement activities. Noise resulting from any military or law enforcement activities of the federal, state or local government;
(7) Construction noises between 7:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m. Noise generated in construction operations between the hours of 7:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m., so long as reasonable steps to abate construction noise are taken;
(8) Landscaping noises between 7:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m. Noise generated by lawn mowers and other landscaping equipment used between the hours of 7:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m. so long as such equipment is in proper working order and equipped with manufacturers' noise reduction equipment;
(9) Bells or chimes from churches, clocks, schools, etc. Noise of any bell or chime which emanates from any church, building clock, school or public building;
(10) Hunting. Noise from dogs and/or firearms while being used in a lawful hunt; and
(11) Firearms used in training, sport shooting. Noise from firearms while being used in law enforcement training or sport shooting such as clay shoots, turkey shoots and the like.
(e) Enforcement. The terms of this article shall be enforced by any and all qualified law enforcement officers and any person so designated by the county board of commissioners. Violations of this article may be prosecuted on accusation or summons in the magistrates court or state court.
(f) Penalty. Violation of this article may be punished according to section 1-13.
(Ord. of 8-3-2006)

